    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="0666" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/621: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gwynn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-31T23:00:00-04:00">July 31, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>121. Your 264, July 26, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Your courtesy visit to Damascus prior to delivery of <hi
                            rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> is approved. However, the
                        Department desires to obtain as early as possible the necessary assurances
                        from the Syrian and Lebanese Governments regarding treatment of American
                        individuals and institutions in Syria and Lebanon, in order that decision
                        may be taken on question of recognition. Note has been taken of your comment
                        in this regard, but consideration of a broad nature connected with our
                        general relations with peoples of the Near East render prompt decision
                        desirable if satisfactory assurances of respect for our treaty rights are
                        received.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Change of wording you suggest in paragraph 2 of <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >aide-mémoire</hi> is approved.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>With reference to your paragraph 7, the Department is not aware of any
                        objection to your continuing to carry on your relations with the Free French
                        authorities in a manner similar to that followed in the past.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
